-- title:
--   Radicality of (q) on the base-changed level model
-- statement:
--   Fix a natural number $N_0 \ne 0$ and a prime $q$ with $q \nmid N_0$, and let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a level-$(N_0,q)$ Deligne–Rapoport model package, i.e. a term of `DRModelPackageLevel N₀ q hqN`: this bundles, for the structural morphism `toBase N₀ q` from the curve `X N₀ q` to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the ring `DRLevel.R q`, properness, flatness, local finite presentation and integrality of the source, integral closedness of $\Gamma(X,U)$ for every affine open $U$, smoothness of relative dimension $1$ and geometric integrality of the generic fibre, a curve model over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ whose function field is the base-changed modular function field of level $N_0 q$ together with an isomorphism onto the corresponding base change, Galois-equivariance and $q$-expansion normalisations, and cusp sections over the base. Let $O$ be a commutative ring, $\rho_O \colon \mathtt{DRLevel.R}\,q \to O$ a ring homomorphism, and assume that the principal ideal generated by the image of the natural number $q$ in $O$ is maximal. Then for every affine open $U$ of the scheme `DRLevel.XO ρO`, the ideal of $\Gamma(\mathtt{DRLevel.XO}\ \rho_O, U)$ generated by $q$ is radical: any section a power of which lies in $q\,\Gamma(U)$ lies in $q\,\Gamma(U)$.
--
--   This is the sectionwise form of the reducedness of the fibre at $q$ of the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_0(N_0 q)$ after base change along $\rho_O$, the residue characteristic being $q$ by the maximality hypothesis. It feeds the crossing-frame analysis of the model used in the level-lowering input [`V3AsmLevel.comp_prod`](thm.html#V3AsmLevel.comp_prod), and the proof cites the reducedness of the geometric fibres of `DRLevel.toBase N₀ q` over algebraically closed fields.
